netstat (win) or ss (Linux) - real-time ports listening or some other states  


The utility that tells you in real-time which ports are in a listening or some other state is netstat or ss, depending on your operating system:

Windows:

netstat -an → Displays all active connections and listening ports.

netstat -ano → Includes the Process ID (PID) for each connection.

netstat -ab → Shows the executable associated with each listening port.

Linux/macOS:

ss -tulnp → Shows listening ports along with process names.

netstat -tulnp (older but still useful) → Displays TCP/UDP ports in use.

For real-time monitoring, you can also use lsof -i (Linux/macOS) or Wireshark for detailed packet analysis.
